title touchstone — one simulation, and every boundary it crosses

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHAT THIS PICTURE IS FOR, AND WHY IT WAS REDRAWN RATHER THAN AMENDED — D-068.
//
//  The old sequence traced cli.py → loop/run.py → agent/graph.py → tools/ →
//  agent/models.py → the claude CLI. Every participant between run.py and the
//  network was OUR agent, and D-062 replaced it with τ²-bench retail. D-066
//  archived the old one whole to `incident-specimen` at 109c424. So five of the
//  eleven participants that survived that redraw are new, and the three that
//  vanished vanished because the files did. ⚠ THE COUNT IS 19 NOW, not eleven —
//  D-082 added six mining-loop lifelines on 2026-08-23. Re-derive it from
//  diagrams/README.md's census command; never step it by hand.
//
//  ⛔ THE RENDERER EATS THREE THINGS AND THE ONLY DEFENCE IS A STATIC GREP.
//     · `note over` renders as NOTHING
//     · an opening `[` in a message label DELETES THE WHOLE MESSAGE
//     · `title` inside a block renders as nothing
//     Milestones 8 and 9 of scripts/check-diagram.py grep the DSL for exactly
//     these. ⛔ Also no ⛔ and no 🔴 in a RENDERED label — a black bar in the
//     flowchart, and ZERO pixels here. They are fine in comments, which is why
//     this block is full of them.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE ONE THING THIS PICTURE EXISTS TO SHOW.
//
//  There are exactly TWO places where touchstone's code sits inside τ²'s control
//  flow, and both are single functions:
//
//    · generate() at llm_utils.py:355 — where the model call is made. The agent,
//      the user simulator and the hallucination reviewer ALL import this one
//      function, so ONE adapter dispatching on `model` covers every role. This is
//      why phase 1 is small, and it was found by reading the imports rather than
//      by assuming a framework shape (rule 7: a mechanism is a claim about the
//      code, and you name the file you read it in).
//
//    · make_tool_call() at environment/environment.py:158 — where a tool actually
//      executes. Every tool call passes through it, and _is_mutating_tool() at
//      :130 has already classified read vs write via toolkit.tool_mutates_state().
//
//  ⚠ THE SECOND ONE IS EMPTY UNTIL PHASE 3. In phase 1 nothing hooks it; in phase
//  2 the gate runs in SHADOW, which means it reads completed sessions and returns
//  no verdict into the flow at all. The `alt` block near the bottom is drawn with
//  the shadow branch as the live one ON PURPOSE — a sequence diagram that shows
//  enforcement working is a diagram of phase 3, and phase 3 has not happened.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  🔴 D-080 AND D-082 MOVED THE CENTRE OF THIS PICTURE. READ THIS BEFORE THE DSL.
//
//  D-080 deferred the OUTER loop entire. τ² is not run by this project at scale any
//  more — every number comes from replaying the 1,712 shipped simulations on disk.
//  The run half below is still drawn because the SEAM is real and P1.0 runs one live
//  simulation as a smoke test, but it is no longer where the results come from.
//  ⛔ `Cmp` therefore has NOTHING TO COMPARE. It is specified in full and it does not
//  run; the alt/else at the bottom is what it revives to, not what happens today.
//
//  D-082 replaced the mining loop's selector with a ROUTER AGENT and named the chain
//  once and for all: router → curator ⇄ critic → run_predicate → admission → suite.
//  That chain is the live half of the project, so it is now drawn here. Three agents
//  propose; `run_predicate()` is the only thing that decides, and it holds no model.
//  ⛔ Its companion picture is diagrams/agents.mmd — same chain, no boundaries.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE TELEMETRY EDGES ARE THE PART THAT CHANGED A DECISION.
//
//  D-063 put the spans on litellm's OTel callback. P1.1 displaces litellm at the
//  seam, so that callback observes nothing — the model calls no longer go through
//  it. touchstone emits its own spans from the adapter, or it has none. Every
//  Tel arrow below comes from OUR code for that reason, and none from litellm.
//
//  ⚠ AND THE REWARD ARRIVES LAST, WHICH CONSTRAINS WHAT A GATE CAN READ. τ²
//  computes the reward AFTER the simulation ends. Spans and labels join at
//  end-of-simulation on session_id. So a gate acting during a run acts on
//  BEHAVIOUR and never on OUTCOME — which is what a gate should do anyway, but
//  it is a consequence of the architecture rather than a preference.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHY THE SCORER HAS NO MODEL IN IT, MEASURED.
//
//  Across the 1,824 shipped simulations of the four public retail runs,
//  reward_breakdown["DB"] is the gating number and the composite is reported beside
//  it — retail declares NL_ASSERTION on 112 of 114 tasks, so the composite carries
//  a judge (D-069). DB is a database-state diff against an annotated goal. The
//  superseded COMMUNICATE component was a
//  lowercased substring match at evaluator_communicate.py:69. No model in either.
//  ⚠ reward_basis is a DECLARATION of what may be scored; reward_breakdown is the
//  EXECUTION RECORD. Reading the first one as the second is how "the NL evaluator
//  is in the reward path for 112 of 114 tasks" got said out loud, and it is wrong.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CLI [icon: terminal, color: blue, label: "cli.py — P0 shipped `doctor`\nP1.6 adds run, score and suite"]
Run [icon: play, color: blue, label: "loop/run.py — the k-attempt driver"]
Orch [icon: repeat, color: grey, label: "τ² Orchestrator.run — orchestrator.py:260\nEXTERNAL, MIT, tau2 at commit a2c024725189"]
Agent [icon: cpu, color: orange, label: "τ² agent — llm_agent.py:128\nTHE THING BEING MEASURED"]
User [icon: user, color: orange, label: "τ² user simulator — user_simulator.py:235\nfrozen apparatus, deliberately NOT the agent's model"]
Gen [icon: git-merge, color: red, label: "generate() — llm_utils.py:355\nthe SINGLE seam: all roles call this one function"]
Adapter [icon: link, color: blue, label: "adapter.py — P1.1\nthe Claude Agent SDK, dispatching on `model`"]
Claude [icon: cloud, color: orange, label: "ClaudeSDKClient to Anthropic\nsubscription auth, five-hour window, the cap REJECTS"]
Env [icon: shield, color: red, label: "make_tool_call() — environment/environment.py:158\nthe enforcement point, empty until phase 3"]
Tel [icon: activity, color: blue, label: "telemetry.py — P1.2\nOUR spans: litellm's callback died with litellm"]
Spans [icon: file-text, color: red, label: "results/spans/(version).jsonl\nthe ONLY thing that crosses from the run to the score"]
Score [icon: bar-chart-2, color: blue, label: "loop/score.py — reads SPANS, never a return value (D-007)"]
Cmp [icon: filter, color: grey, label: "loop/compare.py — P2.4, decision 2\nDEFERRED ENTIRE, D-080 — no second operand exists to compare against"]
Corpus [icon: database, color: grey, label: "tau2-bench results/final/ — 1,712 shipped simulations over 107 tasks\nD-080: the trace source. 834 anomalous, 878 clean, and the clean half is the CONTROL SET"]
Router [icon: git-branch, color: orange, label: "router agent — D-082 §A\nrubric over ONE session: ENHANCE or SKIP. It replaced analyst, the mechanical select, and the unbuilt rubric judge"]
Curator [icon: edit-3, color: orange, label: "curator agent — D-082\nwrites the predicate, and owns the two memories"]
Critic [icon: alert-triangle, color: orange, label: "qa / critic agent — D-082 §C2\nattacks the candidate, and holds run_predicate as its one tool (D-085). MAY bounce on the argument alone, or run first. ONE bounce per attempt"]
Pred [icon: check-square, color: green, label: "run_predicate() — THE ONLY DECISION POINT, D-081\nno model. It fires on the trace, and must be SILENT on the control set"]
Admit [icon: shield, color: green, label: "three admission gates — D-084\nreproducible, distinct, justified. Five were specified; measuring them against 1,824 shipped simulations cut two"]

CLI > Tel: init_telemetry() — ONCE, from cli.py
Tel > Tel: register the exporter BEFORE importing anything that instruments
CLI > Run: touchstone run vN --k 3
Run > Run: read suite/benchmark/manifest.json — TASK IDS and a hash, never task bytes

loop [label: "k attempts — config.K = 3 (D-030) · a cached attempt is never re-run (D-015)"] {
  Run > Orch: run one τ² retail simulation, task_id and seed
  Orch > Tel: touchstone.simulation start — version, task_id, attempt, benchmark_hash

  loop [label: "one conversational turn — until the task ends or the turn cap is hit"] {
    Orch > Agent: the agent's turn
    Agent > Gen: generate(model=MODEL, messages, tools)
    Gen > Adapter: REPLACED here — litellm is no longer on this path
    Adapter > Claude: one model call, the pin for THIS role
    Claude --> Adapter: the assistant message, with usage
    Adapter > Tel: touchstone.model — role, model, tokens, latency. ONE span per call, all four roles
    Adapter --> Gen: an AssistantMessage, the shape τ² already expects
    Gen --> Agent: the turn's output

    opt [label: "the turn contains a tool call"] {
      Agent > Env: make_tool_call — every tool execution passes through here
      Env > Env: _is_mutating_tool at line 130 — τ² already split read from write
      Env > Tel: touchstone.tool — name, mutating, and in phase 3 whether it was REFUSED
      Env --> Agent: the tool result, or in phase 3 a refusal the agent must handle
    }

    Orch > User: the customer's turn
    User > Gen: generate(model=USER_MODEL) — the SAME function, a different pin
    Gen > Adapter: the simulator crosses the identical seam
    Adapter > Claude: haiku, frozen — a correlated apparatus cannot measure what it correlates with
    Claude --> Adapter: the customer's reply
    Adapter --> User: and the conversation continues
  }

  Orch > Orch: evaluate_simulation at evaluator.py:88 — AFTER the run, never during it
  Orch > Tel: touchstone.reward — gates on the DB component of reward_breakdown. No model in that number
  Tel > Spans: the file exporter writes JSONL, timestamps included
}

Score > Spans: read the committed JSONL — NO model call, NO credential (D-014)
Spans --> Score: spans, with their timestamps and the reward joined on session_id
Score > Score: pass^k is the headline, pass@1 beside it — BOTH, especially when they differ
Score > Cmp: results/(version).json — the scored half only. diagnostics reaches nothing (D-045)
Cmp > Cmp: five conditions against the incumbent — an AND, not five options. NOTHING HERE RUNS TODAY

// ── the INNER loop, D-082. This is the half that is live, and it never runs τ². ──
Corpus > Router: one shipped session at a time — ALL 1,712, because the router is what selects now
Router > Curator: ENHANCE — straight to the curator. There is no pre-check, and never was one that worked
Router --> Corpus: SKIP — the session joins the CONTROL SET, which is why the router costs a measured error rate
Router > Router: criterion_1_agreement — the router verdict scored against τ²'s own three signals, over all 1,712. No result is reportable without it

loop [label: "n = 5 attempts on ONE trace — every UNMINEABLE has a run_predicate result behind it"] {
  Curator > Critic: a candidate predicate, and the stated rule it claims to encode
  Critic --> Curator: an ARGUMENT — D-085: MAY come before anything runs, or carry a counterexample the critic ran itself. ONE bounce per attempt
  Critic > Pred: run whatever it has
  Pred > Corpus: fire it against the 878 clean sessions
  Corpus --> Pred: the NO half of the verdict — a hit here is a FALSE POSITIVE
  Pred --> Curator: a COUNTEREXAMPLE, so attempt i+1 sees what attempt i got wrong
  Pred > Pred: record the attempt, the verdict and the counterexample. Giving up is recorded the same way
}

Pred > Admit: it holds on the trace and is silent on the control set
Admit > CLI: admitted to the regression suite, or UNMINEABLE — which is a RESULT, not an error

alt [label: "phase 2 — the gate runs in SHADOW and changes nothing. DEFERRED with compare, D-080"] {
  Cmp --> CLI: the gate's precision and recall, scored against sessions whose outcome is known
}
else [label: "phase 3 — the gate ENFORCES, and the refusal is in the trace. DEFERRED with compare, D-080"] {
  Cmp --> CLI: ACCEPT, or REJECT and WHICH task blocked it. The rejection IS the result
}
